      "pins": ["R6.1", "R6.2", "R9.1", "R9.2", "SW1.1", "SW1.2", "SW2.1", "SW2.2"],
      "nets": ["FLOAT_HIGH", "FLOAT_LOW", "+3V3", "GND"],
      "observed": "R6 (10k) is connected between FLOAT_HIGH and +3V3; R9 (10k) is connected between FLOAT_LOW and GND. SW1 (FLOAT_HIGH) connects to +3V3, and SW2 (FLOAT_LOW) connects to GND.",
      "expected": "Per the design specification, R6 should be a pull-up from FLOAT_LOW to +3V3, and R9 should be a pull-down from FLOAT_HIGH to GND. This allows the float switches to change the signal state.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "R6 FLOAT_LOW +3V3 10k, R9 GND FLOAT_HIGH 10k"},
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "Safety Switches block: R6 10k connected to FLOAT_HIGH and +3V3; R9 10k connected to FLOAT_LOW and GND."}
      ],
      "impact": "FLOAT_HIGH is permanently pulled high and FLOAT_LOW permanently pulled low, so the float switches cannot signal low water or high water. The low-level pump cutoff and high-level overflow protection are defeated.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "category": "wrong_value",
      "components": ["R25", "R27", "R29"],
      "pins": ["R25.1", "R25.2", "R27.1", "R27.2", "R29.1", "R29.2"],
      "nets": ["5VOUT", "VREF", "GND"],
      "observed": "R25, R27, and R29 are labeled '0.7' (0.7 Ω) in the VREF divider from 5VOUT to GND, in series with R24/R26/R28 (4k).",
      "expected": "These should be 0.7 kΩ (or similar high value) to form a proper VREF divider. A 0.7 Ω resistor would draw excessive current from the TMC2209 5VOUT pin and set VREF near 0 V, preventing motor operation.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "Peristaltic Pump Drivers sheet: R25 0.7, R27 0.7, R29 0.7; R24 4k, R26 4k, R28 4k."}
      ],
      "impact": "The TMC2209 VREF will be near 0 V, so the stepper drivers will not drive the peristaltic pumps. The 5VOUT pin may be overloaded.",
      "confidence": 0.9
    },
    {
      "category": "other",
      "components": ["U3", "U4", "R20", "R22", "R21", "R23"],
      "pins": ["U3.13", "U3.14", "U4.13", "U4.14", "R20.1", "R20.2", "R22.1", "R22.2", "R21.1", "R21.2", "R23.1", "R23.2"],
      "nets": ["VISO", "VSEL", "GND", "VDDIO"],
      "observed": "U3 pin 13 (VSEL) is connected to a divider R20 16.9k / R22 10k between VISO and GND, setting VSEL to ~1.86 V. U3 pin 14 (VDDIO) is tied to VISO (5 V). U4 has the same arrangement with R21/R23.",
      "expected": "For 5 V isolated I2C (EZO powered from VISO 5 V, pull-ups to VISO), VSEL should be tied to VISO to select 5 V VDDIO. The divider selects 1.8 V logic, which is incompatible with the 5 V VDDIO and EZO I2C levels.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "pH Sensor block: U3 pin 13 VSEL connected to R20 16k9 and R22 10k; U3 pin 14 VDDIO tied to VISO. EC Sensor block: U4 pin 13 VSEL connected to R21 16k9 and R23 10k; U4 pin 14 VDDIO tied to VISO."},
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "Each isolated EZO channel (U3 for pH, U4 for EC) derives its own isolated +5V (/V_pH, /V_EC) and isolated ground (/GNDISO_pH, /GNDISO_EC) internally from the ADM3260's isoPower feature."}
      ],
      "impact": "The ADM3260 isolated side is configured for 1.8 V I/O while the I/O supply and EZO pull-ups are 5 V. This can cause communication failure or damage to the isolator.",
      "confidence": 0.85
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The schematic contains three significant deviations: the float-switch pull resistors R6 and R9 are swapped, the TMC2209 VREF divider resistors R25/R27/R29 are 0.7 Ω instead of 0.7 kΩ, and the ADM3260 VSEL dividers set 1.8 V logic while VDDIO is tied to 5 V. These would defeat the float safety interlocks, prevent stepper pump operation, and likely break isolated I2C communication."
}

